* /**
*  * @file GIT.HAS
*  * @version 1.0
*  */
* GIT.HAS(name, found) — found = 1 if package `name` is installed via mvpkg, else
* 0.  Cheap: mvpkg's presence is the MVPKG.LOCK record in the account VOC; cache
* that check in COMMON /GITENV/ so VOC is opened at most once per run, and only
* when mvpkg is present defer to the real MVPKG.HAS for the per-package answer.
* Lets GIT pick an installed cmd over its bundled GIT.CMD.* with no catalog games.
SUBROUTINE GIT.HAS(NAME, FOUND)
$INCLUDE BP.INC PLATFORM.H
COMMON /GITENV/ MVPK
FOUND = 0
IF MVPK = "" THEN
   MVPK = "0"
   OPEN MVMASTER TO GHVOC THEN
      READ GHREC FROM GHVOC, "MVPKG.LOCK" THEN MVPK = "1"
   END
END
IF MVPK = "1" THEN CALL MVPKG.HAS(NAME, FOUND)
RETURN